                <pb facs="0714" n="596" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/6438</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-09">September 9, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received October
                        28.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1143</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing my despatch No. 1130 of
                    August 24, 1929, I have the honor to inform the Department that Gabry Rivas and
                    Adan Morales Z. were released from confinement nine days after their arrest on
                    the charge of conspiracy. Investigation of the charge did not produce sufficient
                    evidence to justify a formal accusation against them.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthew E. Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
